-- WARNING: CONCURRENCY -- errors/parallel_shared_write_1.march

Every parallel call writes the same Vault key `"max"`. [parallel_shared_write]

8 |     let _ = List.pmap([3, 9, 4], fn x -> Vault.set(best, "max", x * x))
                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `List.pmap` runs this function on many elements at once, and every call writes the same key `"max"`. The calls finish in no fixed order, so which value is left is a race, and a read-then-write of the key loses updates.
    Return the values from the function and combine the results after the parallel call, or key each write by the element. For a shared counter use `Vault.incr`, which adds under one lock.
    run `march --explain parallel_shared_write`


